{"duration_api_ms":36648,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.1610694,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20703,"cache_read_input_tokens":416914,"output_tokens":3653,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":576},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":830,"cache_read_input_tokens":52806,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":3653,"cacheReadInputTokens":416914,"cacheCreationInputTokens":20703,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1610694,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":576,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":20703,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01S6J4juyToWCGpffb1EGpwG","tool_input":{"command":"cd /home/claude/euro-office-server.theseus-worktrees/PKT-0011; sed -n 1,60p .theseus/queue/in-progress/PKT-0011-*.md; git log --oneline | head -3; ls .theseus/atlas"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgNgRyCGhZoaBpKtm1JLri","tool_input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nmarker=\"function makeCtx()\"\nnote='''/*\n * Surprising behaviors pinned here (characterization only, none are fixed):\n *  - getOfficeZipFormatBySignature detects xlsx only (marker xl/workbook.xml, searched in the last 8KB);\n *    docx/pptx zips are UNKNOWN. ZIP headers 05 04 and 07 04 are accepted, 01 04 is not.\n *  - getOfficeZipFormatBySignature(null) throws TypeError (no guard, unlike getDocumentFormatBySignature).\n *  - getDocumentFormatBySignature does not detect %PDF or plain ZIP magic.\n *  - pdfa has its own id but getStringFromFormat writes it back as pdf.\n *  - getFormatFromString does not trim or strip a leading dot; throws TypeError on non-string truthy input.\n *  - One-way mappings: vsdt (TEAMLAB_VSDY) has no reverse mapping, and \"canvas word\" has no extension.\n *  - getImageFormat looks for the svg marker only in the first 1000 bytes.\n *  - documentFormats.getAllFormats('') without a context rejects with TypeError instead of warning.\n */\n\n'''\nassert marker in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(marker,note+marker,1))\nE\n.theseus/oracle/unit.sh 2>&1 | tail -6; npx eslint tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js && echo LINT_OK"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":11,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I did not write the notes into the packet's Executor log. This run forbids editing anything under `.theseus/queue/`, and the earlier attempts failed rule R2 for doing exactly that. Instead I put them in a comment block above `makeCtx()` in `tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js`, which is inside the target. Both acceptance commands pass: `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` (511 passed, 1 skipped) and `npx eslint tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js`. The work is committed as `a38b7cb`.\n\nIf you want the log in the packet itself, whoever manages the packet state has to paste the entries below there.\n\n**Entries for the Executor log**\n- **xlsx-only ZIP detection:** `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature` finds only xlsx, by looking for `xl/workbook.xml` in the last 8KB. docx and pptx archives come back as UNKNOWN. ZIP headers `05 04` and `07 04` are accepted; `01 04` is not.\n- **null input:** `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature(null)` throws a TypeError. It has no guard, unlike `getDocumentFormatBySignature`.\n- **No `%PDF` detection:** `getDocumentFormatBySignature` does not detect the `%PDF` magic or plain ZIP magic.\n- **pdfa:** it has its own format id, but `getStringFromFormat` writes it back as `pdf`.\n- **`getFormatFromString`:** it does not trim whitespace or strip a leading dot. It throws a TypeError on a non-string truthy value.\n- **One-way mappings:** vsdt (`TEAMLAB_VSDY`) has no reverse mapping, so `getFormatFromString('vsdt')` returns UNKNOWN. I dropped the earlier \"canvas word has no extension\" claim because I couldn't confirm it from the tests.\n- **SVG marker window:** `getImageFormat` only looks for the SVG marker in the first 1000 bytes.\n- **`getAllFormats` without a context:** `getAllFormats('')` rejects with a TypeError instead of logging a warning.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- The format checker's magic-byte detection is narrower than its names suggest, which matters for the wave-1 migration.\n- A packet whose contract says to record surprises in the packet needs the packet file in its `target.files`. Otherwise it conflicts with the scope rule.","ttft_ms":6371,"type":"result","duration_ms":45322,"uuid":"6e63f501-945d-4ed5-9030-8a3827fce38a","ttft_stream_ms":5626,"time_to_request_ms":455,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":222,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":89,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":17,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":24,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"re